412097	412293	412311	412311	He	536	" they will be certain that either Benjamin Bones or John Jeffreys has betrayed them , and they will accordingly give a full and complete explanation , the result of which would be that the whole four would swing together . But I am bound to save Jeffreys from that terrible fate ; and God forbid that that I should be the means , direct or indirect , of sending Benjamin Bones to the scaffold ! And yet , on the other hand , knowing all that I have elicited from Jeffreys , and acting in the true spirit of that mission which I have voluntarily undertaken , I dare not allow this innocent man Torrens to be condemned by a frightful combination of circumstantial evidence , when the utterance of a single word will prove him guiltless and fix the crime on those who really perpetrated it . How stands the matter , then ? Torrens must be saved on the one hand ; but the real murderers must be allowed to escape on the other ! Oh ! this is a fatal necessity — a dreadful alternative ; and yet it is imperious ! "
